#
# Makefile for libatsynmark (run in BUILD/: make -C BUILD -f ../Makefile_build)
#
# HX-2026-10: libatsynmark is written in ATS2 (no GC) and built by patsopt and the C
# compiler alone, on top of the ATS2 sources of the compiler (PATSHOME/src, the
# modules of its lexer, parser and syntax trees). ATS1 is not needed.
#
# libatsynmark.a only holds the objects of libatsynmark: link a program with
#
#   patscc -DATS_MEMALLOC_LIBC -D_GNU_SOURCE -include alloca.h prog.dats \
#     -L$(PATSHOME)/utils/libatsynmark/BUILD -latsynmark -L$(PATSHOME)/src -latsopt -lgmp
#
# where libatsopt.a is the one that `make -C src` (or Makefile_devl, or utils/libatsopt)
# builds; -lgmp is not needed if it was built with C3NSTRINTKND=intknd. Call
# libatsynmark_dynloadall() (see SATS/libatsynmark.sats) first.
#
# Targets: libatsynmark (the default), gen (regenerate the arena encoding of
# libatsynmark.spec), check (typecheck all the files), clean, cleanall
